# WoWAR Project Guidance

- Treat the current code and `WoWAR.toc` as runtime authority.
- Start at `Docs/README.md` and read the maintained document for the subsystem being changed.
- Preserve module ownership and reuse existing helpers, hooks, state, and compatibility bridges.
- Verify patch-dependent Blizzard UI behavior against current documentation or the live client when it is material to the change.
- Run the relevant scenarios in `Docs/RegressionTesting.md`.
- Update maintained Markdown when architecture, ownership, settings, rendering contracts, or required tests change.
- Keep session scratchpads, journals, generated indexes, and local vector databases out of the project documentation.
